##Question 1 – Dealer-wise Renewal Performance
1. Business scenario
You are working as a Data Analyst at an insurance company.
Your manager wants to analyse the renewal performance of different dealers for January 2026.
You have been given two tables:
Table 1: Dealers
Table name: Dealers
Column name	Data type	Description
dealer_id	INT	Unique dealer ID
dealer_name	VARCHAR	Dealer name
branch	VARCHAR	Branch name

Sample data:
dealer_id	dealer_name	branch
101	Honda Motors	Dehradun
102	TVS Automobiles	Haridwar
103	Royal Enfield	Nainital
104	Suzuki Motors	Dehradun

Table 2: Policies
Table name: Policies
Column name	Data type	Description
policy_id	INT	Unique policy ID
dealer_id	INT	Dealer ID
customer_id	INT	Customer ID
expiry_date	DATE	Policy expiry date
policy_status	VARCHAR	Renewed / Pending
premium	DECIMAL	Policy premium amount

Sample data:
policy_id	dealer_id	customer_id	expiry_date	policy_status	premium
1001	101	501	2026-01-05	Renewed	5000
1002	101	502	2026-01-12	Pending	6000
1003	101	503	2026-01-20	Renewed	4500
1004	102	504	2026-01-08	Pending	7000
1005	102	505	2026-01-15	Renewed	5500
1006	103	506	2026-01-18	Renewed	8000
1007	103	507	2026-01-25	Pending	6500
1008	104	508	2026-02-05	Renewed	4000


2. Your task
Your manager wants a dealer-wise renewal performance report for January 2026.

Write a SQL query to extract the following information:
1. dealer_name
2. branch
3. total_expiring_policies – Total policies expiring in January 2026.
4. renewed_policies – Number of policies successfully renewed.
5. pending_policies – Number of policies still pending.
6. total_premium – Total premium of policies expiring in January.
7. renewal_percentage – Calculate the renewal percentage.

Important conditions
- Include all four dealers, even if a dealer has no policies expiring in January.
- Consider only policies expiring between 1 January and 31 January 2026.
- Do not count February policies.
- Avoid NULL values in your calculated output.
- Sort the result by renewal percentage in descending order.

##Sqlcode
WITH renewal_cte AS
(
    SELECT
        d.dealer_name,
        d.branch,
        COUNT(p.policy_id) AS total_expiring_policies,
        COUNT(CASE
            WHEN p.policy_status = 'Renewed' THEN 1
        END) AS renewed_policies,
        COUNT(CASE
            WHEN p.policy_status = 'Pending' THEN 1
        END) AS pending_policies,
        COALESCE(SUM(p.premium), 0) AS total_premium
    FROM Dealers d
    LEFT JOIN Policies p
        ON d.dealer_id = p.dealer_id
        AND p.expiry_date >= '2026-01-01'
        AND p.expiry_date < '2026-02-01'
    GROUP BY
        d.dealer_name,
        d.branch
)
SELECT
    dealer_name,
    branch,
    total_expiring_policies,
    renewed_policies,
    pending_policies,
    total_premium,
   COALESCE(
        100.0 * renewed_policies /
        NULLIF(total_expiring_policies, 0),
        0
    ) AS renewal_percentage
FROM renewal_cte
ORDER BY
    renewal_percentage DESC,
    dealer_name ASC;
